Problem：
How can I effectively organize my daily study time to balance schoolwork, exercise, and rest?

Applying Computational Thinking：
1. Decomposition
Break the big problem into smaller parts.
I divide my daily schedule into three main parts: study time, exercise time, and rest time. Then I further break study time into different subjects.
2. Pattern Recognition
Find patterns or similarities in the problem.
I notice that I am most focused in the morning, and I get tired after lunch. Also, I feel sleepy if I study for more than 45 minutes without a break.

